  "sourceInstructions": "<root xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-works/ProductModelManuInstructions\">AI-generated fictional demo instructions. Not validated engineering or safety instructions. Chain Stays (Product Number CS-2812) part sheet. Fictional shop-floor demonstration for manufacturing Chain Stays, product 324 (CS-2812), from its direct raw-material component.<Location LocationID=\"10\" SetupHours=\"0.2\" LaborHours=\"0.5\" MachineHours=\"0.25\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 10 - Frame Forming. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Forming: prepare and form the raw material into a schematic chain-stay shape.<step>For one finished part, collect 1.00 EA of <material>Metal Sheet 5 (Product Number MS-2341)</material> and visually check it for obvious damage.</step><step>Using an <tool>assumed sheet-cutting tool</tool>, prepare a blank for forming. The illustrated shape is only a demo assumption; see illustration <diag>2003241</diag>.</step><step>Form the blank using an <tool>assumed forming jig and press</tool>; set the formed piece aside for edge finishing.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"30\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.25\" MachineHours=\"0\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 30 - Debur and Polish. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Debur and Polish: finish exposed edges and visually check the formed part.<step>Remove obvious burrs from the formed piece with an <tool>assumed hand deburring tool</tool>.</step><step>Visually check for sharp edges, cracks and obvious distortion; separate any questionable piece for review.</step></Location></root>",
